/*
 * broker - broker-wide state, session lifetime and QoS 0 message fan-out.
 *
 * Threading model
 * ---------------
 * One broker_t is created before the listener starts and is destroyed only
 * after every session object has been freed (broker_wait_all() followed by
 * broker_destroy()).  Every accepted peer is represented by one session_t that
 * is owned by exactly one detached worker thread (conn_main) from
 * broker_session_new() until that worker calls broker_session_free().  If the
 * creating thread cannot start the worker it must free the session itself with
 * broker_session_free().
 *
 * Functions marked "owner thread only" may be called exclusively by the worker
 * that owns the session; they touch unsynchronized fields.  Functions marked
 * "any thread" use the session's internal locks or the broker mutex.
