src/conn.c/conn_process_input
Framing loop over the session input accumulator: repeatedly mqtt_frame_decode the buffered bytes, consume exactly header_len bytes on MQTT_DECODE_INVALID (then close), consume header_len bytes and dispatch on a complete fixed header once total_len bytes are buffered, keep MQTT_DECODE_INCOMPLETE buffered, close on MQTT_DECODE_NOMEM or on buffered bytes above CONN_MAX_BUFFERED, and with eof set process all remaining complete frames before reporting that the truncated tail must be discarded.

src/conn.c/conn_handle_subscribe
Validate with mqtt_subscribe_begin (INVALID closes the connection without a SUBACK), then iterate the payload pairs with mqtt_subscribe_next in order, storing each validated filter with broker_subscribe (granted QoS 0) and recording one 0x00 return code per pair, and finally enqueue a single SUBACK carrying the SUBSCRIBE packet identifier and the ordered codes; MQTT_SUB_NEXT_INVALID, an allocation failure or a SUBACK enqueue failure closes the connection.

