LOGIC/EVENT: {"TRIGGER":"POLL_OUT is reported for a peer whose poll snapshot included POLLOUT because its output FIFO was nonempty.","PRECONDITION":"client fd is explicitly O_NONBLOCK; output_head non-NULL; only writable readiness may dispatch send. Caller must not call recv here. client remains listed during this call.","INPUT":"A FIFO of complete owned wire packet buffers; each head has length and sent cursor where 0<=sent<length.","ACTION":"While output_head exists, compute remaining=length-sent and call send(fd,bytes+sent,remaining,MSG_NOSIGNAL). Retry EINTR. If positive n, advance sent by exactly n; if sent reaches length, unlink head, if it was tail set tail=NULL, then free its bytes and node exactly once, and continue with next queued node using the same POLLOUT readiness. If send returns EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK, stop and retain head bytes/cursor and return 0 so poll requests POLLOUT again. Zero return or any other error returns -1 for peer-local cleanup. After FIFO becomes empty, if close_after_write is set return 1; otherwise return 0. No blocking calls, no read, and no busy retry on would-block.","STATE_CHANGE":"A successful partial send advances only current node's sent cursor. A complete send transfers no ownership externally and frees current node/buffer; FIFO head/tail advance. Queued close-after-response peer is closed only when all queued bytes are sent.","RESPONSE":"No new packet is created. Return 0 for open peer (queue may be empty), 1 for drained close-after-write peer, -1 for send failure.","EVENT_TYPE":"writable readiness output progress","INVARIANTS_USED":["Only POLLOUT permits send dispatch.","Writable readiness never permits a blocking read.","Partial writes retain unsent suffix in owned FIFO.","Idle recipients receive output because POLLOUT requested independent of POLLIN.","MSG_NOSIGNAL prevents peer reset from terminating process.","Every completed or removed buffer is freed exactly once."]}
