F11 Clean Session CONNECT session lifetime When CleanSession=1, Client and Server discard any previous Session and start a new one; this Session lasts only as long as the Network Connection, and its state must not be reused in a later Session.
F12 Successful CONNACK The first packet sent by the Server to a Client must be CONNACK. CONNACK has type 2, fixed flags 0000, Remaining Length 2, one acknowledgement-flags byte and one return-code byte. Reserved acknowledgement bits are zero; for an accepted CleanSession=1 connection, Session Present is zero and the success return code is zero.
