ject. Close client->fd exactly once and mark it invalid if fields are retained during destruction. Free client->input exactly once even when input_len is zero but allocated capacity is nonzero; resetting length alone is not release. For each subscription node, save next, free its owned copied filter (even if logical length is zero), then free node; do not free any filter bytes borrowed from a parsed packet because stored filters must always be copied. For each output node, save next, free its owned complete frame buffer regardless of partial-send offset, then free node. These loops also handle empty lists and partially populated queues after prior failures. Free client itself last. No other client's descriptor, subscriptions, input or queue is touched.", "OUTPUT": "No return value. The target is removed from the shared list and its descriptor, retained input allocation, every copied filter allocation and subscription node, every queued output byte buffer and node, and the client object have each been released once.", "INVARIANTS_USED": ["R10/F11/F22: all subscription/session state is scoped to this TCP connection and cannot be inherited by a new client.", "R12: each stored filter/output/input allocation has one owner; freeing a logical length is not equivalent to releasing allocated storage; teardown releases old owners exactly once.", "F21: peer-local error cleanup does not affect unrelated clients."], "PRECONDITION": "Target appears exactly once in the list and has not previously been passed to remove_client; list head and object remain valid. Poll traversal has already stopped using this object.", "POSTCONDITION": "Target is absent from clients and all its owned resources are released; no other client state changed.", "IDEMPOTENT": false, "THREAD_SAFETY": "Called serially by broker poll-loop owner only."}
